onfigurations; Experimental protocol) and Supplementary Information Table hyper/devfinal): No retained artifact shows which configuration was frozen or that it was evaluated only once. The final manifest path in paper_data.json does not resolve in the workspace. V2 and V3 tie exactly at 0.9192069392814439, so the score cannot tell them apart. The sealed metrics are tied to V2's source only by that claim and by the ordering of top_programs.\n  - claim: V2 \"is the configuration recorded by the selection manifest\"; the studied procedure \"is the configuration frozen by the selection step and evaluated on sealed data\"; \"evaluated once on sealed cases\"\n  - evidence: paper.tex Method sections \"Compared configurations\" and \"Experimental protocol\"; claims_grounding.json claim \"Final seeds 9001-9005 ... frozen procedure evaluated once on sealed cases\" cites only final.evidence.episodes and result.top_program_01; paper_data.json top_programs lists c02 (V2) and c03 (V3) with identical scores; final_evaluation.manifest_path is not present; scientific-evidence/ledger.jsonl is empty.\n  - requested_fix: State that the sealed evaluation is attributed to the V2 configuration on the basis of its position in the development ranking (tied with V3), and that the selection manifest is not retained. Remove or qualify \"recorded by the selection manifest\" and \"evaluated once\". Add a limitation that the frozen configuration's identity is not independently verified.\n- `intro-close-to-nominal` (Introduction (answer paragraph)): The only evidence is a one-sided under-coverage gap of 0.0017, averaged over a few seeded runs. The paper's own Results and Method sections say this gap does not show that coverage is tight, and over-coverage is not measured. \"Close to nominal\" is therefore stronger than the evidence and conflicts with the later caveat.\n  - claim: the procedure \"also remains close to nominal marginal coverage on exchangeable cases\"\n  - evidence: paper.tex Introduction; Results \"Reliability profile\" (\"this is not a test of the guarantee and does not show coverage is tight\"); Method on one-sided gaps; claims_grounding.json claim \"Exchangeable-case marginal under-coverage gap is 0.0017\"; evaluator score_sets uses max(0, 1-alpha-cov).\n  - requested_fix: Reword to \"shows a small one-sided marginal under-coverage gap (0.0017) on exchangeable cases\". Do not describe coverage as close to nominal or tight.\n- `conclusion-marginal-largest-contributor` (Conclusion): The marginal term (0.0893) is not measured. It is obtained by subtracting the size and slice terms from the mean loss, and alpha and per-case results are not retained. claims_grounding.json labels it \"implied\", and Results hedges it. The Conclusion drops that qualifier and states it as an identified result.\n  - claim: the loss decomposition \"identifies marginal under-coverage as the largest residual contributor\"\n  - evidence: derived/derived_stats.json final_loss_decomposition (\"marginal term obtained by subtraction\"); claims_grounding.json loss-decomposition claim (\"implied marginal term\"); paper.tex Results (\"we cannot establish this without per-case results\"); figure loss_decomposition legend \"Marginal term (implied)\".\n  - requested_fix: Change the Conclusion to say the decomposition implies, by subtraction under the evaluator's aggregation, that the marginal term is the largest component. Keep the caveat that alpha and per-case results are unavailable.\n# Draft reference gap memo\n\n**Status:** ready (3 targets). No retrieval was run in this stage.\n\n## Summary\nRelated work cites many peripheral conformal papers (class-conditional, efficiency, time series, clinical applications). It does not cite the foundational and directly-used sources: the baseline score functions, split/Mondrian conformal, and weighted conformal under covariate shift. `references.bib` contains no Vovk, Romano, Angelopoulos, Tibshirani (weighted) or Aitchison entries. The appendix already acknowledges that these are \"stated as background without citation\".\n\n## Missing literatures\n- Split (inductive) and Mondrian conformal prediction foundations\n- Weighted conformal prediction under covariate shift\n- Conformal classification scores (LAC, APS, RAPS)\n- Compositional data analysis (Aitchison log-ratio geometry)\n\n## Targets\n\n1. **baseline-score-sources** (high, comparator) — Method, \"Baselines, negative controls and validity conditions\". The headline claim is a margin over the best of LAC/APS/RAPS/class-wise LAC, yet none of these is cited. Search: LAC / least-ambiguous set classifiers; APS; RAPS; class-wise split conformal.\n2. **mondrian-split-conformal-foundations** (high, background) — Method, \"Statistical background\". The Proposition and rank argument are called textbook but unsourced, and Mondrian calibration is the core of the method. Search: Mondrian conformal prediction (Vovk et al.); split/inductive conformal; distribution-free finite-sample coverage.\n3. **weighted-conformal-shift-and-compositional-framing** (medium, positioning) — Method, \"Weighted calibration under covariate shift\", and Related Work, \"Positioning\". The gated weighting step and the shift axis lack their source (weighted conformal under covariate shift; classifier-based density ratios). The log-ratio compositional framing is uncited. Search: conformal under covariate shift; probabilistic-classifier density-ratio estimation; Aitchison compositional data.\n\n## Deliberately ignored\n- Quantitative results (grounded in `paper_data.json`).\n- Further applied or tutorial conformal papers, and the existing Related Work paragraphs on other output types.\n- Real-data or CIFAR-10 literature, which would require reshaping the paper's synthetic-only scope.\nfigures:\nfinal_comparison.pdf\nfinal_comparison.pdf.prov.json\nfinal_comparison.png\nfinal_comparison.png.prov.json\nloss_decomposition.pdf\nloss_decomposition.pdf.prov.json\nloss_decomposition.png\nloss_decomposition.png.prov.json\nposthoc\nprotocol_overview.png\nprotocol_overview.png.prov.json\nprotocol_overview.prompts.json\nvariant_profile.pdf\nvariant_profile.pdf.prov.json\nvariant_profile.png\nvariant_profile.png.prov.json\n\nscientific-evidence:\nbundle.manifest.json\nledger.jsonl\nschemas\nspec.md\nverification-report.json","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
