    {\n      \"claim\": \"the loss decomposition \\\"identifies marginal under-coverage as the largest residual contributor\\\"\",\n      \"evidence\": \"derived/derived_stats.json final_loss_decomposition (\\\"marginal term obtained by subtraction\\\"); claims_grounding.json loss-decomposition claim (\\\"implied marginal term\\\"); paper.tex Results (\\\"we cannot establish this without per-case results\\\"); figure loss_decomposition legend \\\"Marginal term (implied)\\\".\",\n      \"fix\": \"Change the Conclusion to say the decomposition implies, by subtraction under the evaluator's aggregation, that the marginal term is the largest component. Keep the caveat that alpha and per-case results are unavailable.\",\n      \"id\": \"conclusion-marginal-largest-contributor\",\n      \"issue\": \"The marginal term (0.0893) is not measured. It is obtained by subtracting the size and slice terms from the mean loss, and alpha and per-case results are not retained. claims_grounding.json labels it \\\"implied\\\", and Results hedges it. The Conclusion drops that qualifier and states it as an identified result.\",\n      \"section\": \"Conclusion\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-11-11T10:25:21.999448+00:00\",\n  \"ok\": false,\n  \"raw_output_path\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/paper/paper_evidence_audit_raw.txt\",\n  \"summary\": \"Numbers and tables match paper_data.json, derived_stats.json, the V1-V3 metrics files and the evaluator source, and the qualified outcome is reported correctly. Three wording or grounding gaps remain: the frozen-configuration identity, the \\\"close to nominal\\\" coverage claim, and the loss-decomposition conclusion.\",\n  \"verdict\": \"fail\"\n}-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   9323 2026-11-11 10:20:16.921369191 +0000 claims_grounding.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   4389 2026-11-11 10:23:34.615888885 +0000 figure_manifest.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent 422197 2026-11-11 10:23:39.352897466 +0000 paper.pdf\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent  46338 2026-11-11 10:23:10.314445183 +0000 paper.tex\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   4843 2026-11-11 10:25:21.999983995 +0000 paper_evidence_audit_feedback.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   9909 2026-11-11 10:25:22.104654027 +0000 validation_feedback.md\n45:The answer we can support is conditional. On sealed final data the studied procedure obtains a higher composite score than the best of four evaluator-implemented baselines, with a paired margin whose bootstrap interval excludes zero; it also remains close to nominal marginal coverage on exchangeable cases. At the same time, the sealed metrics show non-trivial residual under-coverage on shifted cases and on worst slices, and the retained artifacts do not allow us to say which baseline was best, which cases drive the residual gaps, or whether the result extends beyond the declared families.\n85:For one episode with set indicator $\\mathcal C(x_j)$ on $n$ test points, let $\\mathrm{cov}$ be empirical coverage, $\\rho=\\frac1{nK}\\sum_j|\\mathcal C(x_j)|$ the set-size ratio, and $g_{\\mathrm{m}}=\\max(0,1-\\alpha-\\mathrm{cov})$ the one-sided marginal gap. The worst-slice gap $g_{\\mathrm{s}}$ is the largest one-sided coverage shortfall over slices with at least 30 test points: classes when $K\\le10$, and strata of set size and of maximum probability (quartiles) when $K>10$. The episode loss and score are\n132:\\paragraph{Development data.} V1--V3 are scored with seeds 101--103 on the evaluator's development cases (per the declared reset sequence, three seeds on each of four case designs, plus the three controls); all three configurations produced valid runs and none was unscored. The development score of V2 and V3 tie exactly, and V2 is the configuration recorded by the selection manifest.\n133:\\paragraph{Sealed final data.} The frozen procedure is evaluated once on sealed cases with seeds 9001--9005, disjoint from the development data by content hash. Each seeded run's score is the mean over cases of $1-\\ell$; the reported final score is the equal-weight mean over seeds and cases. Development and final numbers use different cases and seeds and are never pooled.\n177:This subtraction relies on the evaluator aggregating the components exactly as reported, and $\\alpha$ is not retained, so we do not convert it to a coverage number. Since exchangeable-case gaps are small, the marginal term is plausibly dominated by shifted cases, but we cannot establish this without per-case results. The largest single residual cost is therefore marginal under-coverage, not set size. We do not attribute the residual shift or slice gaps to statistical noise, to the density-ratio estimation, or to a validity failure of the weighting: no gate-level diagnostics are retained.\n224:We studied a Mondrian least-ambiguous-set conformal procedure with a gated, cross-fitted domain-classifier reweighting step under a multi-axis reliability protocol on synthetic softmax families. On sealed final data it reached a composite score of 0.8416 versus 0.8029 for the best of four standard baselines, a paired margin of 0.0387 with a bootstrap 95\\% interval of 0.0274--0.0499, with no failed episodes and all negative controls passed. The same evaluation shows that the procedure does not remove under-coverage under shift (0.0536) or on worst slices (0.0675), and the loss decomposition identifies marginal under-coverage as the largest residual contributor. The conclusions are conditional on the declared synthetic families, on one aggregated best-baseline comparison, and on evaluator-defined weights. The most useful next steps are per-case and per-baseline reporting, ablations that isolate the gate and the weighting from the Mondrian grouping, gate-activation logging, and an evaluation on real classifier outputs; none of these has been done here.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"529359a3-cd47-4a89-a29c-a6a024fe0bef","uuid":"4421cc05-29ef-4704-b0d5-265e27ea1c22","timestamp":"2026-11-11T10:25:32.782Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"figures\": [\n    {\n      \"caption_short\": \"Evaluation protocol at a glance\",\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 8.0,\n      \"figure_id\": \"protocol_overview\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"diagram\",\n      \"files\": {\n        \"png\": \"figures/protocol_overview.png\"\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"min_font_size_pt\": 8.0,\n      \"panel_count\": 1,\n      \"panels\": [\n        {\n          \"category_count\": 6,\n          \"content\": \"simplex outputs -> conformal procedures -> three score axes + negative controls\",\n          \"label\": \"Protocol overview\",\n          \"panel_id\": \"a\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"prompt_log_path\": \"figures/protocol_overview.prompts.json\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"source_ids\": [],\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"caption_short\": \"Sealed final comparison\",\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 7.5,\n      \"figure_id\": \"final_comparison\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"dot_plot_with_interval\",\n      \"files\": {\n        \"pdf\": \"figures/final_comparison.pdf\",\n        \"png\": \"figures/final_comparison.png\"\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 0.95,\n      \"min_font_size_pt\": 7.5,\n      \"panel_count\": 2,\n      \"panels\": [\n        {\n          \"category_count\": 1,\n          \"label\": \"Paired margin with 95% bootstrap interval\",\n          \"metric\": \"score_margin_vs_best_baseline\",\n          \"panel_id\": \"a\",\n          \"series_count\": 1\n        },\n        {\n          \"category_count\": 5,\n          \"label\": \"Per-seed final scores\",\n          \"metric\": \"final_score\",\n          \"panel_id\": \"b\",\n          \"series_count\": 3\n        }\n      ],\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.metric.score_margin_vs_best_baseline\",\n        \"final.metric.score_margin_ci_lower\",\n        \"final.metric.score_margin_ci_upper\",\n        \"final.metric.final_score\",\n        \"final.metric.best_baseline_score\",\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"caption_short\": \"Development comparison of nested configurations\",\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 6.0,\n      \"figure_id\": \"variant_profile\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"small_multiples_dot_plot\",\n      \"files\": {\n        \"pdf\": \"figures/variant_profile.pdf\",\n        \"png\": \"figures/variant_profile.png\"\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 0.8,\n      \"min_font_size_pt\": 6.0,\n      \"panel_count\": 4,\n      \"panels\": [\n        {\n          \"category_count\": 3,\n          \"label\": \"Shift-case marginal gap\",\n          \"panel_id\": \"a\",\n          \"series_count\": 1\n        },\n        {\n          \"category_count\": 3,\n          \"label\": \"Worst-slice gap\",\n          \"panel_id\": \"b\",\n          \"series_count\": 1\n        },\n        {\n          \"category_count\": 3,\n          \"label\": \"Set-size ratio\",\n          \"panel_id\": \"c\",\n          \"series_count\": 1\n        },\n        {\n          \"category_count\": 3,\n          \"label\": \"Per-seed development score\",\n          \"panel_id\": \"d\",\n          \"series_count\": 1\n        }\n      ],\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"result.improvement_001\",\n        \"result.improvement_002\",\n        \"result.top_program_02\",\n        \"result.top_program_03\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"caption_short\": \"Decomposition of the sealed final mean loss\",\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 6.0,\n      \"figure_id\": \"loss_decomposition\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"bar\",\n      \"files\": {\n        \"pdf\": \"figures/loss_decomposition.pdf\",\n        \"png\": \"figures/loss_decomposition.png\"\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 0.78,\n      \"min_font_size_pt\": 6.0,\n      \"panel_count\": 1,\n      \"panels\": [\n        {\n          \"category_count\": 2,\n          \"label\": \"Final mean loss decomposition\",\n          \"panel_id\": \"a\",\n          \"series_count\": 4\n        }\n      ],\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.metric.final_score\",\n        \"final.metric.best_baseline_score\",\n        \"final.metric.mean_set_size_ratio\",\n        \"final.metric.worst_slice_coverage_gap\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    }\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"audit_json_path\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/paper/paper_evidence_audit.json\",\n  \"audit_markdown_path\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/paper/paper_evidence_audit.md\",\n  \"finding_count\": 3,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"V2 \\\"is the configuration recorded by the selection manifest\\\"; the studied procedure \\\"is the configuration frozen by the selection step and evaluated on sealed data\\\"; \\\"evaluated once on sealed cases\\\"\",\n      \"evidence\": \"paper.tex Method sections \\\"Compared configurations\\\" and \\\"Experimental protocol\\\"; claims_grounding.json claim \\\"Final seeds 9001-9005 ... frozen procedure evaluated once on sealed cases\\\" cites only final.evidence.episodes and result.top_program_01; paper_data.json top_programs lists c02 (V2) and c03 (V3) with identical scores; final_evaluation.manifest_path is not present; scientific-evidence/ledger.jsonl is empty.\",\n      \"fix\": \"State that the sealed evaluation is attributed to the V2 configuration on the basis of its position in the development ranking (tied with V3), and that the selection manifest is not retained. Remove or qualify \\\"recorded by the selection manifest\\\" and \\\"evaluated once\\\". Add a limitation that the frozen configuration's identity is not independently verified.\",\n      \"id\": \"frozen-config-identity-ungrounded\",\n      \"issue\": \"No retained artifact shows which configuration was frozen or that it was evaluated only once. The final manifest path in paper_data.json does not resolve in the workspace. V2 and V3 tie exactly at 0.9192069392814439, so the score cannot tell them apart. The sealed metrics are tied to V2's source only by that claim and by the ordering of top_programs.\",\n      \"section\": \"Method (Compared configurations; Experimental protocol) and Supplementary Information Table hyper/devfinal\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"the procedure \\\"also remains close to nominal marginal coverage on exchangeable cases\\\"\",\n      \"evidence\": \"paper.tex Introduction; Results \\\"Reliability profile\\\" (\\\"this is not a test of the guarantee and does not show coverage is tight\\\"); Method on one-sided gaps; claims_grounding.json claim \\\"Exchangeable-case marginal under-coverage gap is 0.0017\\\"; evaluator score_sets uses max(0, 1-alpha-cov).\",\n      \"fix\": \"Reword to \\\"shows a small one-sided marginal under-coverage gap (0.0017) on exchangeable cases\\\". Do not describe coverage as close to nominal or tight.\",\n      \"id\": \"intro-close-to-nominal\",\n      \"issue\": \"The only evidence is a one-sided under-coverage gap of 0.0017, averaged over a few seeded runs. The paper's own Results and Method sections say this gap does not show that coverage is tight, and over-coverage is not measured. \\\"Close to nominal\\\" is therefore stronger than the evidence and conflicts with the later caveat.\",\n      \"section\": \"Introduction (answer paragraph)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"the loss decomposition \\\"identifies marginal under-coverage as the largest residual contributor\\\"\",\n      \"evidence\": \"derived/derived_stats.json final_loss_decomposition (\\\"marginal term obtained by subtraction\\\"); claims_grounding.json loss-decomposition claim (\\\"implied marginal term\\\"); paper.tex Results (\\\"we cannot establish this without per-case results\\\"); figure loss_decomposition legend \\\"Marginal term (implied)\\\".\",\n      \"fix\": \"Change the Conclusion to say the decomposition implies, by subtraction under the evaluator's aggregation, that the marginal term is the largest component. Keep the caveat that alpha and per-case results are unavailable.\",\n      \"id\": \"conclusion-marginal-largest-contributor\",\n      \"issue\": \"The marginal term (0.0893) is not measured. It is obtained by subtracting the size and slice terms from the mean loss, and alpha and per-case results are not retained. claims_grounding.json labels it \\\"implied\\\", and Results hedges it. The Conclusion drops that qualifier and states it as an identified result.\",\n      \"section\": \"Conclusion\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-11-11T10:25:21.999448+00:00\",\n  \"ok\": false,\n  \"raw_output_path\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/paper/paper_evidence_audit_raw.txt\",\n  \"summary\": \"Numbers and tables match paper_data.json, derived_stats.json, the V1-V3 metrics files and the evaluator source, and the qualified outcome is reported correctly. Three wording or grounding gaps remain: the frozen-configuration identity, the \\\"close to nominal\\\" coverage claim, and the loss-decomposition conclusion.\",\n  \"verdict\": \"fail\"\n}-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   9323 2026-11-11 10:20:16.921369191 +0000 claims_grounding.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   4389 2026-11-11 10:23:34.615888885 +0000 figure_manifest.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent 422197 2026-11-11 10:23:39.352897466 +0000 paper.pdf\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent  46338 2026-11-11 10:23:10.314445183 +0000 paper.tex\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   4843 2026