{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017C5yBtt9FTwizUrC4Pwut5","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n \"$defs\": {\n  \"FigureFontSizes\": {\n   \"additionalProperties\": false,\n   \"description\": \"Explicit font sizes for the legacy manifest contract.\",\n   \"properties\": {\n    \"axis\": {\n     \"title\": \"Axis\",\n     \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"legend\": {\n     \"title\": \"Legend\",\n     \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"ticks\": {\n     \"title\": \"Ticks\",\n     \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"title\": {\n     \"title\": \"Title\",\n     \"type\": \"number\"\n    }\n   },\n   \"required\": [\n    \"title\",\n    \"axis\",\n    \"ticks\",\n    \"legend\"\n   ],\n   \"title\": \"FigureFontSizes\",\n   \"type\": \"object\"\n  },\n  \"LegacyFigureManifestFigure\": {\n   \"additionalProperties\": false,\n   \"allOf\": [\n    {\n     \"else\": {\n      \"properties\": {\n       \"path_pdf\": {\n        \"minLength\": 1\n       }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n       \"path_pdf\"\n      ]\n     },\n     \"if\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"properties\": {\n         \"generator\": {\n          \"const\": \"generate-concept-figure\"\n         }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n         \"generator\"\n        ]\n       },\n       {\n        \"properties\": {\n         \"attempted_generator\": {\n          \"const\": \"generate-concept-figure\"\n         },\n         \"fallback_reason\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n         },\n         \"generator\": {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n         },\n         \"prompt_log_path\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n         }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n         \"generator\",\n         \"attempted_generator\",\n         \"prompt_log_path\",\n         \"fallback_reason\"\n        ]\n       }\n      ]\n     }\n    }\n   ],\n   \"description\": \"Original flat figure-manifest entry shape.\",\n   \"properties\": {\n    \"attempted_generator\": {\n     \"anyOf\": [\n      {\n       \"enum\": [\n        \"generate-concept-figure\",\n        \"matplotlib\",\n        \"tikz\",\n        \"native_latex\",\n        \"manual\"\n       ],\n       \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"type\": \"null\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"default\": null,\n     \"title\": \"Attempted Generator\"\n    },\n    \"categories_per_panel\": {\n     \"items\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n     },\n     \"title\": \"Categories Per Panel\",\n     \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": {\n     \"anyOf\": [\n      {\n       \"exclusiveMinimum\": 0,\n       \"type\": \"number\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"type\": \"null\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"default\": null,\n     \"title\": \"Estimated Min Rendered Font Pt\"\n    },\n    \"fallback_reason\": {\n     \"anyOf\": [\n      {\n       \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"type\": \"null\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"default\": null,\n     \"title\": \"Fallback Reason\"\n    },\n    \"figure_id\": {\n     \"minLength\": 1,\n     \"title\": \"Figure Id\",\n     \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"figure_type\": {\n     \"enum\": [\n      \"grouped_bar\",\n      \"bar\",\n      \"line\",\n      \"box\",\n      \"violin\",\n      \"scatter\",\n      \"heatmap\",\n      \"table_matrix\",\n      \"table\",\n      \"composite\",\n      \"diagram\"\n     ],\n     \"title\": \"Figure Type\",\n     \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"font_sizes\": {\n     \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FigureFontSizes\"\n    },\n    \"generator\": {\n     \"anyOf\": [\n      {\n       \"enum\": [\n        \"generate-concept-figure\",\n        \"matplotlib\",\n        \"tikz\",\n        \"native_latex\",\n        \"manual\"\n       ],\n       \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"type\": \"null\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"default\": null,\n     \"title\": \"Generator\"\n    },\n    \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": {\n     \"anyOf\": [\n      {\n       \"exclusiveMinimum\": 0,\n       \"maximum\": 1,\n       \"type\": \"number\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"type\": \"null\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"default\": null,\n     \"title\": \"Intended Latex Width Fraction\"\n    },\n    \"max_label_chars\": {\n     \"exclusiveMinimum\": 0,\n     \"title\": \"Max Label Chars\",\n     \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"n_panels\": {\n     \"exclusiveMinimum\": 0,\n     \"title\": \"N Panels\",\n     \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"panels_per_row\": {\n     \"exclusiveMinimum\": 0,\n     \"title\": \"Panels Per Row\",\n     \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"path_pdf\": {\n     \"default\": \"\",\n     \"title\": \"Path Pdf\",\n     \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"path_png\": {\n     \"minLength\": 1,\n     \"title\": \"Path Png\",\n     \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"placement\": {\n     \"anyOf\": [\n      {\n       \"enum\": [\n        \"column\",\n        \"full_width\"\n       ],\n       \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"type\": \"null\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"default\": null,\n     \"title\": \"Placement\"\n    },\n    \"prompt_log_path\": {\n     \"anyOf\": [\n      {\n       \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"type\": \"null\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"default\": null,\n     \"title\": \"Prompt Log Path\"\n    },\n    \"series_per_panel\": {\n     \"items\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n     },\n     \"title\": \"Series Per Panel\",\n     \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"source_ids\": {\n     \"items\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n     },\n     \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n     \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"uses_abbrev_labels\": {\n     \"title\": \"Uses Abbrev Labels\",\n     \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"uses_progression\": {\n     \"title\": \"Uses Progression\",\n     \"type\":\n257:    \"manifest_path\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json\",\n285:      \"manifest_path\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json\",\n295:      \"manifest_path\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json\",\n303:      \"manifest_path\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json\",\n311:      \"manifest_path\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json\",\n319:      \"manifest_path\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json\",\n327:      \"manifest_path\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json\",\n335:      \"manifest_path\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json\",\n343:      \"manifest_path\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json\",\n351:      \"manifest_path\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json\",\nWe studied a Mondrian least-ambiguous-set conformal procedure with a gated, cross-fitted domain-classifier reweighting step under a multi-axis reliability protocol on synthetic softmax families. On sealed final data it reached a composite score of 0.8416 versus 0.8029 for the best of four standard baselines, a paired margin of 0.0387 with a bootstrap 95\\% interval of 0.0274--0.0499, with no failed episodes and all negative controls passed. The same evaluation shows that the procedure does not remove under-coverage under shift (0.0536) or on worst slices (0.0675), and the loss decomposition identifies marginal under-coverage as the largest residual contributor. The conclusions are conditional on the declared synthetic families, on one aggregated best-baseline comparison, and on evaluator-defined weights. The most useful next steps are per-case and per-baseline reporting, ablations that isolate the gate and the weighting from the Mondrian grouping, gate-activation logging, and an evaluation on real classifier outputs; none of these has been done here.\n\n% IMPORTANT: \\clearpage flushes all pending floats before references so that\n% body-page counting excludes reference-only pages.  Do NOT remove.\n\\clearpage\n\\bibliography{references}\n\\bibliographystyle{paper}\n\n\\clearpage\n\\appendix\n\\section{Supplementary Information}\n\n\\subsection{Procedure specification}\nTable~\\ref{tab:hyper} lists the constants of the studied procedure as they appear in its source, and Algorithm-style pseudo-code follows.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/V2/program.py#constants]]\n\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Constants of the studied procedure (from the frozen configuration's source).}\n\\label{tab:hyper}\n\\begin{tabular}{llr}\n\\toprule\nComponent & Constant & Value \\\\\n\\midrule\nScore & nonconformity & $1-p_k(x)$ \\\\\nMondrian & class-conditional if & $K\\le10$ \\\\\nMondrian & confidence bins ($K>10$): max bins / min rows per bin & 10 / 80 \\\\\nMargin & pooled / per-group multiplier $z$ & 0.7 / 0.6 \\\\\nShrinkage & pseudo-count $n_0$ toward pooled threshold & 20 \\\\\nGate & min. test rows before domain fit & 40 \\\\\nGate & weights used only if $\\beta>$ & $10^{-3}$ \\\\\nDomain classifier & ridge penalty / cross-fit folds / features $d$ & 1 / 2 / 5 \\\\\nWeights & clip range (multiplicative) & $[1/8,\\,8]$ \\\\\nFeatures & standardised clip & $\\pm8$ \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}\n\n\\paragraph{Pseudo-code.}\nclaims_grounding.json:126:   \"claim\": \"Final seeds 9001-9005 and development seeds 101-103; frozen procedure evaluated once on sealed cases.\",\npaper.tex:128:\\emph{Baselines} are the four evaluator-implemented split-conformal procedures above; only the best baseline score and the paired margin are retained. \\emph{The studied procedure} is Mondrian LAC with gated weighting; it is the configur\npaper.tex:133:\\paragraph{Sealed final data.} The frozen procedure is evaluated once on sealed cases with